Spec: Delivery Layer
Purpose: Securely and reliably transmit transformed and encrypted records from the local PostgreSQL database to external target systems.

Platform: Go/Linux

Structure:
  ./mitm_delivery_apigee/
  ./mitm_delivery_cority/
  ./migrations/
  ./docs/

Owns:
  ./**

References:
  ./delivery_concept.md

Must:
  Strictly separate logging concerns: system_logs for lifecycle/errors, job_audit_logs for processing metrics, admin_audit_logs for manual triggers/config changes.
  Batch pending records into Delivery Packages.
  Generate a unique Idempotency-Key for every package.
  Persist packages into a central `delivery_outbox` table (Outbox Pattern).
  Implement an Exponential Backoff retry engine for transient network errors.
  Move permanently failed packages to a Dead Letter Queue (DLQ).
  Target endpoints and credentials are provided to the batch job dynamically at runtime.
